          <a href="/contact/" class="hero__cta hero__cta--primary">Get Free Quote</a>
          <a href={`${WHATSAPP_URL}?text=Hi%20SDF%20Clothing%2C%20I%20need%20help%20with%20my%20startup%20brand`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="hero__cta hero__cta--secondary">WhatsApp Now</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero__stats">
        <div class="hero__stat">
          <span class="hero__stat-value">300</span>
          <span class="hero__stat-label">Pieces Minimum</span>
        </div>
        <div class="hero__stat">
          <span class="hero__stat-value">Low</span>
          <span class="hero__stat-label">MOQ Startup</span>
        </div>
        <div class="hero__stat">
          <span class="hero__stat-value">{companyAge}</span>
          <span class="hero__stat-label">Years Experience</span>
        </div>
        <div class="hero__stat">
          <span class="hero__stat-value">Scale</span>
          <span class="hero__stat-label">Ready</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="trust">
    <div class="trust__container">
      <div class="trust__items">
        <div class="trust__item">
          <span class="trust__icon">✓</span>
          <span>Low MOQ Production</span>
        </div>
        <div class="trust__item">
          <span class="trust__icon">✓</span>
          <span>Brand Development</span>
        </div>
        <div class="trust__item">
          <span class="trust__icon">✓</span>
          <span>Tech Pack Support</span>
        </div>
        <div class="trust__item">
          <span class="trust__icon">✓</span>
          <span>Scaling Path</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Startup Challenges</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Specific Challenges Clothing Startups Face</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Clothing startups face unique challenges that established brands have already overcome. The most significant hurdle is finding manufacturers willing to work with low order quantities. Most traditional garment factories require minimum orders of 1,000-5,000 pieces per style, creating an impossible barrier for new brands testing their first collections. This MOQ challenge forces many startups to either compromise on quality by working with less capable manufacturers or invest heavily in inventory before validating market demand.</p>
        
        <p>Beyond MOQ challenges, startups struggle with production timeline management, quality control without established relationships, fabric selection without industry connections, and cash flow management for production costs. These challenges compound each other—delays in production can miss selling seasons, quality issues damage brand reputation before it's established, and poor fabric choices lead to customer returns. Many startups underestimate the complexity of manufacturing and focus primarily on design, only to encounter production realities that can derail their launch plans.</p>
        
        <p>SDF Clothing addresses these startup-specific challenges through our low MOQ model, comprehensive support systems, and startup-friendly approach. Our 300-piece minimum enables market testing without excessive inventory investment. Our experience working with hundreds of startups means we understand the typical pitfalls and provide proactive guidance to avoid them. We've structured our entire operation to support new brands through their critical first collections and beyond.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">How SDF Helps</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">How SDF Helps New Clothing Brands</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>SDF Clothing provides comprehensive support specifically designed for new clothing brands. Our approach goes beyond simple manufacturing to include guidance and services that address the full spectrum of startup needs. We understand that new brands need more than just production—they need a partner who has actually done the work of bringing a clothing line to market before and can walk them through it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="comparison-wrapper">
        <table class="comparison">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Support Area</th>
              <th>What We Provide</th>
              <th>Startup Benefit</th>
              <th>Timeline</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="comparison__row--highlight">
              <td>Tech Pack Development</td>
              <td>Review and refinement of technical specifications</td>
              <td>Manufacturable designs, reduced revisions</td>
              <td>Pre-production</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Fabric Sourcing</td>
              <td>Fabric recommendations and sourcing assistance</td>
              <td>Appropriate materials, cost optimization</td>
              <td>Pre-production</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Sampling</td>
              <td>Prototype development and fit testing</td>
              <td>Design validation, market feedback</td>
              <td>2-3 weeks</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="comparison__row--highlight">
              <td>Production Planning</td>
              <td>Timeline and scheduling management</td>
              <td>Launch alignment, reduced delays</td>
              <td>Ongoing</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Quality Control</td>
              <td>Inspection and testing protocols</td>
              <td>Consistent quality, reduced returns</td>
              <td>Production</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Scaling Strategy</td>
              <td>Growth planning and capacity management</td>
              <td>Sustainable growth, volume benefits</td>
              <td>Post-launch</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
          <caption>Support services available as needed. Startups can select services based on their specific requirements.</caption>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Minimum Requirements</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Minimum Requirements for Working with SDF</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>We've intentionally minimized our requirements to make manufacturing accessible to new brands. Unlike many manufacturers who require annual volume commitments, established business history, or complex qualification processes, SDF works with brands at any stage from concept to established business. Our requirements focus on the essentials needed to produce quality garments rather than arbitrary barriers to entry.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="comparison-wrapper">
        <table class="comparison">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Requirement</th>
              <th>What We Need</th>
              <th>What We Don't Need</th>
              <th>Flexibility</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="comparison__row--highlight">
              <td>Design Documentation</td>
              <td>Basic sketches or tech pack concepts</td>
              <td>Professional tech packs not required</td>
              <td>High</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Quantity Commitment</td>
              <td>300 pieces per style</td>
              <td>No annual volume commitment</td>
              <td>High</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Business History</td>
              <td>None required</td>
              <td>No track record needed</td>
              <td>High</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="comparison__row--highlight">
              <td>Timeline</td>
              <td>Target delivery date</td>
              <td>Rush production available</td>
              <td>Medium</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Payment</td>
              <td>Deposit and balance</td>
              <td>No long-term contracts</td>
              <td>Medium</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
          <caption>Requirements designed to be startup-friendly. We accommodate brands at all development stages.</caption>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Brand Development</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Brand Development Support</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Brand development support at SDF focuses on helping startups translate their creative vision into manufacturable reality. Many new brands have strong design concepts but lack technical manufacturing knowledge. Our team bridges this gap, providing guidance that ensures designs can be produced efficiently while maintaining brand aesthetics. This support prevents costly revisions and production delays that commonly occur when designs aren't optimized for manufacturing.</p>
        
        <p>Design consultation services include reviewing sketches for manufacturability, suggesting construction methods that balance aesthetics with production efficiency, and recommending fabric choices that achieve desired performance within budget constraints. Our pattern makers and sample makers work directly with startup teams to refine designs before production, catching potential issues early when changes are least costly. This collaborative approach helps startups learn manufacturing considerations while developing their collections.</p>
        
        <p>Fabric selection guidance leverages our extensive supplier network and material knowledge. We help startups navigate fabric options based on their target market, price point, and performance requirements. This includes explaining trade-offs between different fabric types, suggesting alternatives that achieve similar aesthetics at different price points, and providing samples for evaluation. Our fabric expertise helps startups make informed decisions that balance quality, cost, and brand positioning.</p>
      </div>
