  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Scaling Path</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Scaling Path for Growing Brands</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Scaling with SDF follows a structured path designed to support brands through their growth stages. We understand that startup needs evolve from initial launch to established growth, and our services adapt accordingly. The scaling path begins with low MOQ production for market testing, progresses to increased volumes as demand validates, and eventually accommodates large-scale production for established brands.</p>
        
        <p>The initial launch phase typically involves 300-500 pieces per style for market testing. This phase focuses on validating designs, gathering customer feedback, and establishing brand presence. Our production during this stage emphasizes flexibility and quick turnaround to enable rapid iteration based on market response. Pricing at this stage reflects the lower volumes but provides access to professional manufacturing quality that wouldn't be possible with domestic or smaller-scale alternatives.</p>
        
        <p>As brands establish market demand and sales performance, scaling increases to 1,000-2,000 pieces per style. At this volume, pricing becomes more competitive, and production efficiency improves. Our capacity accommodates this growth while maintaining the same quality standards and communication that established during the startup phase. Brands benefit from volume pricing while continuing to work with a manufacturing partner who understands their products and brand identity.</p>
        
        <p>For established brands requiring 5,000+ pieces per style, we offer dedicated production lines, priority scheduling, and further pricing optimization. At this scale, we can implement specialized processes, custom fabric developments, and dedicated quality control protocols. The relationship evolves from startup support to strategic partnership, with our team contributing to seasonal planning, inventory management, and long-term production strategy.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
